#!/usr/bin/env bash
#MISE description="Gate: a PR body that defers a decision without naming the issue that owns it (reads the body on stdin; pointer-only)"
#
# CLOUD-323. AGENTS.md: "what you decline to fix, you file", and a punt is "any
# deferral you could have closed". `issue-guard` gates STARTING work with no key.
# Nothing gated FINISHING work that leaves a decision open — so two open
# decisions landed on `main` during CLOUD-164 with their only record a paragraph
# in a PR body (CLOUD-321, CLOUD-322). A PR body is not a durable home: nothing
# sweeps merged bodies, and the board showed a clean Done with no follow-up.
#
# THE OBVIOUS PREDICATE IS REFUTED, AND THAT IS WHY THIS IS PARAGRAPH-SCOPED.
# "A deferral phrase and no CLOUD key in the body" fires on ZERO of the 60 most
# recent merged PRs, because `issue-guard` already forces a key onto every one.
# Body-level key presence carries no information. What discriminates is whether
# the deferral's OWN paragraph names the issue that owns it — measured:
#
#   judgement call   1 firing, 0 false positives          KEEP
#     fires:  #243 "UUID became a 256-bit minted hex id"  (the real untracked one)
#     exempt: #233's override paragraph, which names CLOUD-164 beside it
#   worth checking   2 firings, both false positives      DROP
#     both are review prompts about implemented, tested properties — the
#     post-merge review this repo runs on purpose, not a deferral
#   deliberate(ly)   16 firings                           DROP
#     this repo's word for a justified choice; gating it would desensitise the
#     whole channel, which is what CLOUD-245 warns about
#   undecided / needs a decision / awaiting review    0   DROP
#     never written here; a branch nothing exercises is the dead code CLOUD-235
#     already cost this repo
#
# ONE SHAPE, because one is what survived measurement. Thin evidence, and stated
# as such: one firing over sixty PRs, the same order as CLOUD-252's single true
# positive, accepted on the argument that a shape firing once correctly beats one
# that never fires. Re-measure as the corpus grows.
#
# NOT A CLASSIFIER (non-negotiable rule 3). This never decides whether prose
# MEANS a deferral. It asks whether a named literal appears with no key beside
# it, which is a computable predicate over text. The escape is honest and cheap:
# name the owning issue, or do not use the phrase.
#
# POINTER, NEVER PAYLOAD (rule 4): the paragraph's first line as a coordinate,
# never the paragraph. Handing the prose back would let the finding be cleared by
# REWORDING it, the mirror hazard `finding-sink-check`'s header records.
#
# The chat-side sibling is deliberately absent. CLOUD-322 never reached a PR body
# at all — it was stated in a message and written nowhere — and
# `stop-posture-check` misses it because its literals match HEDGED framing while
# that sentence was confident. That shape must be measured over the transcript
# corpus before any literal is added, and CLOUD-323 carries it.
#
# `.claude/rules/toolchain.md` is the authority on where this sits among the
# guards, and it is updated in the same change: `issue-guard` gates the start,
# this gates the finish.
set -euo pipefail

# The one shape, and the key that exempts it.
DEFERRALS="judgement call|judgment call"
KEY="CLOUD-[0-9]+"

body=$(cat) || exit 0
[ -n "$body" ] || exit 0

violations=0
report() { # pointer-only: a coordinate, never the prose
	echo "$1" >&2
	violations=$((violations + 1))
}

# Paragraphs, not lines. `RS=""` is awk's paragraph mode — blank-line separated,
# runs of blank lines collapsed, which is the paragraph notion a human writing
# markdown has — emitted NUL-delimited, and `read -d ''` to match — NOT a bare `read`, which
# splits on NEWLINES and would make every LINE its own "paragraph". Measured: the
# line-split version fired on #233, whose deferral names CLOUD-164 on a different
# line of the same paragraph, so the gate disagreed with the measurement it was
# built from. Reproducing the corpus is what caught it.
paragraph=0
while IFS= read -r -d '' para; do
	paragraph=$((paragraph + 1))
	# `-o` on a here-string, never `producer | grep -q`: under pipefail an
	# early-exiting grep in a pipeline promotes a MATCH to a failure status
	# (pipefail-grep-check).
	hit=$(grep -oiE "$DEFERRALS" <<<"$para" || true)
	[ -n "$hit" ] || continue
	owner=$(grep -oE "$KEY" <<<"$para" || true)
	[ -n "$owner" ] && continue
	# The paragraph's first line, trimmed to a coordinate length. Enough to find
	# it; not enough to be a mirror of it.
	first=$(head -n 1 <<<"$para" | cut -c1-60)
	report "paragraph:${paragraph} deferral-without-owner (${first})"
done < <(tr -d '\r' <<<"$body" | awk 'BEGIN { RS = ""; ORS = "\0" } { print }')

[ "$violations" -eq 0 ] && {
	echo "deferral-check: every deferral names the issue that owns it"
	exit 0
}

cat <<'REASON' >&2
::error:: deferral-check: a deferred decision has no ticket.

A PR body is not a durable home — nothing sweeps merged bodies, and the board is
what others read. File the decision as a `CLOUD-*` issue and name it in the same
paragraph, so the deferral and its owner travel together.

If the paragraph is not a deferral, say so without the phrase.
REASON
exit 1
